tween two new interfaces (LANA=vtnet1/10.50.10.1 facing node2, LANB=vtnet2/10.50.20.1 facing node3), added firewall pass rules for both, and added a single hybrid-mode outbound SNAT rule (source 10.50.10.0/24, interface opt2/LANB) that translates node2->node3 traffic to node1's LANB address (10.50.20.1) while leaving node3->node2 traffic un-NATed. Verified with real TCP connections in both directions, then completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart/recovery protocol on all three nodes, confirming changed boot identities and full functional recovery of the asymmetric NAT behavior afterward.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Discovered topology: node1 (OPNsense) vtnet0 shares mgmt network with node2/node3 eth0; vtnet1/vtnet2 unconfigured and paired to node2/node3 eth1 respectively\",\"Assigned static IPs 10.50.10.2/24 (node2 eth1) and 10.50.20.2/24 (node3 eth1), added cross routes via node1\",\"Persisted node2/node3 eth1 IP+route via /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts ifcfg/route files (RHEL7 network-scripts)\",\"Edited /conf/config.xml on node1 to add opt1 (LANA, vtnet1, 10.50.10.1/24) and opt2 (LANB, vtnet2, 10.50.20.1/24) interfaces; ran /usr/local/etc/rc.reload_all to apply\",\"Added firewall pass rules for opt1 and opt2 interfaces (default-deny would otherwise block)\",\"Switched outbound NAT to hybrid mode and added an SNAT rule (from 10.50.10.0/24, interface opt2) translating source to node1's LANB address only for LANA->LANB traffic; fixed initial XML field-name bug (source/destination -> from/to) required by SNatRule.php parser\",\"Opened temporary firewalld test ports on node2/node3, ran python TCP client/server tests confirming NAT applies only in the LANA->LANB direction and not the reverse, then removed the temporary ports and test scripts\",\"Captured pre-restart boot identity (kern.boottime on node1, boot_id on node2/node3) and health baselines\",\"Rebooted node2, node3, then node1 one at a time via native reboot commands, polled until each came back, and confirmed changed boot identity for each\",\"Re-verified interfaces, NAT rule, firewall rules and routes survived reboot on all nodes, and re-ran the TCP test end-to-end post-restart to confirm functional recovery of the required NAT behavior\",\"Cleaned up all test scripts, log files, and temporary firewalld port rules\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node2 (lan-a) -> node3 (lan-b) connection observed by node3 as arriving from a node1 address, not node2's own address\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e072fa5b9f0a4a34\",\"cmd-7bf2310f5f0b4bbf\",\"cmd-f99826db6b85453e\"],\"summary\":\"TCP client on node2 (src 10.50.10.2) connected to node3:5001; node3's peer.log recorded the connecting address as ('10.50.20.1', 3038) -- node1's LANB-facing address, confirmed by the active pf NAT rule 'nat on vtnet2 inet from 10.50.10.0/24 to any -> (vtnet2:0)'\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 (lan-b) -> node2 (lan-a) connection keeps its original source address\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f13cdd2aea624f56\",\"cmd-9223c69a649745e8\"],\"summary\":\"TCP client on node3 connected to node2:5002; node2's peer.log recorded the connecting address as ('10.50.20.2', 38722) -- node3's real, unmodified address\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 baseline health before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a384a92a252d4ce5\"],\"summary\":\"Captured kern.boottime and confirmed pf NAT rule + interface addresses present before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-21d8b572169848e4\",\"cmd-018167e1dd534fb2\",\"cmd-c77780021bb045e7\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command returned before disconnect; kern.boottime changed from 17:16:59 to 17:24:44; post-restart pfctl output shows interfaces, pass rules, and the SNAT rule all intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 functional recovery proof (NAT behavior still correct after restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a1377423e1f2497d\",\"cmd-cc948a018a1c413a\",\"cmd-90e22d0127c14e2e\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart TCP test: node2->node3 connection observed by node3 as arriving from 10.50.20.1 (node1's LANB address), confirming the asymmetric NAT still functions after node1's reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 baseline health before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fe2ce9e40d7b462a\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id and confirmed eth1 static IP and route to 10.50.20.0/24 present before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-79d13705a66a4158\",\"cmd-3b59f1d014d349cc\",\"cmd-0b308c9d272a4323\"],\"summary\":\"shutdown -r now issued and connection dropped as expected; boot_id changed from 738d0aac-71a1-4191-8a37-bf00edfeff5d to 413c9405-5467-46f6-9390-7803742e1603 with fresh uptime; eth1 IP and route to 10.50.20.0/24 recovered via persisted ifcfg/route files\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 baseline health before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0e3e974f75f8436e\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id and confirmed eth1 static IP and route to 10.50.10.0/24 present before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f994fa465d93435d\",\"cmd-f19497dd134b48ba\",\"cmd-68ee61c0030f4e35\"],\"summary\":\"shutdown -r now issued and connection dropped as expected; boot_id changed from 2fc81aed-3ce8-4a35-8f4c-b73206afa45f to 2186f308-6e5f-477d-8cbd-e297643a281d with fresh uptime; eth1 IP and route to 10.50.10.0/24 recovered via persisted ifcfg/route files\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 (OPNsense) to route between two new interfaces (LANA=vtnet1/10.50.10.1 facing node2, LANB=vtnet2/10.50.20.1 facing node3), added firewall pass rules for both, and added a single hybrid-mode outbound SNAT rule (source 10.50.10.0/24, interface opt2/LANB) that translates node2->node3 traffic to node1's LANB address (10.50.20.1) while leaving node3->node2 traffic un-NATed. Verified with real TCP co